wireview-linux (1.4.1.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WireView Mini: an entry in the application launcher. It starts
    WireView Mini and opens its control panel in the browser, or opens the
    running one's control panel (wireview-mini --launch); its Control panel
    action runs wireview-mini --open.
  * WireView Mini: a second copy started while one runs exits with "already
    running" in the ahead-of-time build too. The single-instance lock is a
    file lock next to settings.json instead of a named mutex, which that
    build does not honour.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:44:39 +0000

wireview-linux (1.4.0.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WireView Mini, /usr/bin/wireview-mini: a program with no window that
    owns the device, raises fault alerts, shuts the PC down on a fault when
    set and publishes the device on the LAN while the app is closed. Its
    tray icon and its control panel in the browser cover monitoring,
    charts, the device log with CSV export, device configuration and
    profiles, the theme editor, firmware flashing and wireviewd's settings.
    wireview-mini --install starts it at login.
  * The app connects through WireView Mini while it runs and borrows the
    serial port from it for flashing, log reads and theme transfers.
  * Device log: a cycle's clock starts at its first sample, so the second
    sample no longer pushes the cycle days ahead.
  * Theme editor: translucent background images are no longer darkened.
  * Recommends wireview-hwmon 1.8.1 or later, whose wireviewd takes the
    LAN port back from WireView Mini on its own.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:54:24 +0000

wireview-linux (1.3.2.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Software rendering by default on Linux, about half the resident memory;
    Settings, Startup, GPU rendering switches back at the next start, and
    WIREVIEW_RENDER_MODE overrides both.
  * The background photo is decoded at the screen's width, ICU is dropped,
    the GC runs non-concurrent with ConserveMemory, and a compacting
    collection runs when the window hides to the tray.
  * wireview-linux --page monitoring opens on a given page.

 -- Emanuele Sparvoli <sparvoli@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:46:57 +0000

wireview-linux (1.3.1.1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * udev rule: the serial port keeps the distro's own serial group (dialout,
    or uucp on Arch-based distros), so the rule works when installed
    unchanged. The DFU bootloader's group is on a line of its own (#5).

